summary:
  Any failed play marks the device's row "Cannot play this station", a
  device that is switched off among them.

history:
  The row's words are a statement about the station: the device answered
  and turned its address down. A speaker that is off, a television that did
  not take the stream in time or a missing library say nothing of the
  kind, and "Cannot play this station" on their rows would send a listener
  looking for another station when the device needs switching on.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      else if (kind === "refused") s.refused[uuid] = true;

replace:
      else s.refused[uuid] = true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_only_a_refusal_of_the_address_marks_a_device.
